{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7553348","formula":"Na₃O₃PS","hill":"Na3O3PS","elements":["O","Na","P","S"],"composition":{"O":3.0,"P":1.0,"S":1.0,"Na":3.0},"names":{"en":"Sodium monothiophosphate","ru":"Монотиофосфат натрия"},"descriptions":{"en":"Sodium monothiophosphate, or sodium phosphorothioate, is an inorganic compound with the chemical formula Na3PO3S. It is a sodium salt of monothiophosphoric acid (H3PO3S). Sodium monothiophosphate forms hydrates Na3PO3S·xH2O. The anhydrous form and all hydrates are white solids. The anhydrous salt (x = 0) (Na3PO3S) decomposes without melting at 120-125 °C. More common is the dodecahydrate (Na3PO3S·12H2O).","ru":"Монотиофосфа́т на́трия — неорганическое соединение, соль натрия и монотиофосфорной кислоты с формулой Na3PO3S, бесцветные кристаллы, растворяется в воде, образует кристаллогидраты."},"fame":13,"pubchemCid":9877537,"mass":180.01,"charge":0,"smiles":"[O-]P(=S)([O-])[O-].[Na+].[Na+].[Na+]","inchikey":"RIFYBBXGYKFBFC-UHFFFAOYSA-K","iupac":"trisodium;thiophosphate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-542136","atoms":60,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[8.512,0.0,0.0],[-4.256,7.372,0.0],[0.0,0.0,11.855]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":2.945,"y":5.065,"z":2.278,"el":"Na"},{"x":2.654,"y":0.018,"z":2.278,"el":"Na"},{"x":7.17,"y":2.289,"z":2.278,"el":"Na"},{"x":5.598,"y":4.747,"z":0.302,"el":"Na"},{"x":1.602,"y":2.475,"z":0.302,"el":"Na"},{"x":5.568,"y":0.15,"z":0.302,"el":"Na"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.915,"z":6.801,"el":"P"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.915,"z":0.874,"el":"P"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.915,"z":2.976,"el":"S"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.915,"z":8.904,"el":"S"},{"x":2.777,"y":2.484,"z":2.383,"el":"O"},{"x":4.972,"y":1.163,"z":2.383,"el":"O"},{"x":5.019,"y":3.725,"z":2.383,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.763,"y":6.182,"z":0.407,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.716,"y":3.62,"z":0.407,"